      "description": "A group of well-wishers of the RSS has registered with the US Department of Justice as a foreign agent of the organisation with an aim to step up outreach in the US.\nThe RSS Friends, which provided a Georgia address in the registration document, listed Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh, Keshavkunj, New Delhi as its \"foreign principal\".\nThe RSS Friends registered with the Department of Justice under the Foreign Agents Registration Act (FARA) on August 27.\nCorrecting or responding to information that RSS Friends believes is inaccurate, incomplete, or lacking relevant context is also listed among proposed activities.\n\"RSS Friends does not have a written employment, consulting, lobbying, public-relations, or agency agreement with RSS containing specified deliverables, compensation, or detailed operational instructions,\" the group said.\nIt said the absence of a written contract should not be understood as a representation that no relationship, request, understanding, coordination, authorisat",
